{:paths ["src" "resources" "lib" "examples" "ontology" "vendor/src" "vendor/resources"]
 ;; mithril does not depend on kotoba-lang.
 ;;
 ;; Everything in :deps below used to be a git pin on
 ;; https://github.com/kotoba-lang/<repo>.git. Those repositories were removed
 ;; when kotoba-lang consolidated all of its code into the
 ;; kotoba-lang/kotoba-lang monorepo, so every one of these pins stopped
 ;; resolving ("Error building classpath. Unable to clone
 ;; https://github.com/kotoba-lang/io-ipld.git: could not read Username") and
 ;; took the codegraph gate down with it.
 ;;
 ;; The code is now committed here, under vendor/, as a pinned snapshot that
 ;; this repository owns. Nothing in the build clones, fetches, or calls a
 ;; kotoba-lang repository, package registry, or service. Per-file provenance
 ;; (source repository, source revision, source path, SHA-256) is in
 ;; vendor/PROVENANCE.json; vendor/PROVENANCE.md explains the layout.
 ;;
 ;; The namespaces are unchanged, so no :require form in mithril source moved.
 ;; The pin rationale is kept verbatim below because it is design history; the
 ;; revision each note refers to is recorded in vendor/PROVENANCE.json.
 ;;
 ;;   org-w3-json-ld-api ef6a81a: only a STRING is IRI-coerced under @type @id
 ;;   (§5.3.2), so the Form writes native integers / booleans on IRI keys as
 ;;   they are. It includes 70058cc, which defines a term's prefix before
 ;;   expanding it (JSON-LD 1.1 §4.2.2). Earlier pins left rdfs:subClassOf /
 ;;   domain / range / sh:* / mith:name as literal compact strings in predicate
 ;;   position whenever the map walk reached the term before its prefix. Floor.
 ;;   nquads.core/parse, which mithril.reason uses for .nq/.nt data. Floor.
 ;;
 ;;   oak 4474497: oak.semantic/entail -- the complete OWL 2 RL table that
 ;;   mithril.reason runs; 2-arity materialize (the domain modules) is
 ;;   unchanged. Floor.
 ;;
 ;;   org-w3-owl2 93214e9: owl.rl + owl.rules/supported-rules /
 ;;   supported-vocabulary / vocabulary-status (the capability seam). Same sha
 ;;   oak pins. Floor.
 ;;
 ;;   kotobase-client: verified GET/PUT /ipld/:cid client for opt-in remote
 ;;   reason evidence.
 ;;   io-ipld-car: CAR selection and trustless replay for portable CID history
 ;;   proofs.
 ;;   kotobase-protocol-ipq: the same IPQ/1 handler backs the loopback HTTP
 ;;   interoperability test.
 :deps {}}